      "RWR",
      "[Expert R1] (Detect atomicity violations in the code.)\n```json\n{\n    \"violations\": [\n        {\n            \"sharedVariable\": \"j\",\n            \"accessPattern\": [\"Read\", \"Write\", \"Read\"],\n            \"lines\": [14, 20, 14]\n        }\n    ]\n}\n```\n\n[System] Expert first round completed in 2.81 seconds\n\n[Judge R1] (Validate the expert's defect report and check control/interrupt conditions.)\nLet me analyze the accessibility of each read/write operation involving the global variable `j`.\n\n## Analysis of Read/Write Operations for Variable `j`\n\n### 1. Read operation at line 14: `i = j + 1;`\n- **Location**: `svp_simple_332_001_isr_1`, inside a for loop\n- **Control condition**: `k < NUM` where `k` starts at 0 and increments by 1 each iteration\n- **Variable value tracking**: `k` is initialized to 0 at line 13 and increments by 1 in each loop iteration\n- **Execution path**: The loop will execute exactly NUM (20) times, so this read operation will execute 20 times\n- **Interrupt status**: No interrupt disable/enable calls in the program, so interrupts are always enabled\n- **Conclusion**: This read operation can be executed\n\n### 2. Write operation at line 20: `j = i + 1;`\n- **Location**: `svp_simple_332_001_isr_2`, inside a for loop\n- **Control condition**: `k < NUM` where `k` starts at 0 and increments by 1 each iteration\n- **Variable value tracking**: `k` is initialized to 0 at line 19 and increments by 1 in each loop iteration\n- **Execution path**: The loop will execute exactly NUM (20) times, so this write operation will execute 20 times\n- **Interrupt status**: No interrupt disable/enable calls in the program, so interrupts are always enabled\n- **Conclusion**: This write operation can be executed\n\n### 3. Read operation at line 14: `i = j + 1;` (second occurrence)\n- This is the same read operation as the first one, just appearing again in the access pattern\n- **Conclusion**: This read operation can be executed (same reasoning as above)\n\n## Summary of Analysis\nAll three operations in the reported violation can be executed:\n- The read at line 14 (in isr_1) can execute 20 times\n- The write at line 20 (in isr_2) can execute 20 times\n- The read at line 14 (in isr_1) can execute again\n\nSince both ISRs can preempt each other (no interrupt disabling), and both loops execute 20 times, the atomicity violation involving variable `j` is valid.\n\n```json\n{\n    \"violations\": [\n        {\n            \"sharedVariable\": \"j\",\n            \"accessPattern\": [\"Read\", \"Write\", \"Read\"],\n            \"lines\": [14, 20, 14]\n        }\n    ]\n}\n```\n\n[Expert R2] (Refine the report based on judge feedback, re-check for missed or false defects.)\n```json\n{\n    \"violations\": [\n        {\n            \"sharedVariable\": \"j\",\n            \"accessPattern\": [\"Read\", \"Write\", \"Read\"],\n            \"lines\": [28, 20, 28]\n        }\n    ]\n}\n}\n```\n\n"
    ],
    "expert_task_2": [
      "WRW",
      "[Expert R1] (Detect atomicity violations in the code.)\n```json\n{\n    \"violations\": [\n        {\n            \"sharedVariable\": \"i\",\n            \"accessPattern\": [\"Write\", \"Read\", \"Write\"],\n            \"lines\": [14, 20, 14]\n        }\n    ]\n}\n```\n\n[System] Expert first round completed in 2.76 seconds\n\n[Judge R1] (Validate the expert's defect report and check control/interrupt conditions.)\nLet me analyze each read/write operation for the global variable `i` to determine if the reported atomicity violation can actually occur.\n\n## Step 1: Check Control Conditions\n\n### Operations in svp_simple_332_001_isr_1:\n- **Line 14**: `i = j + 1;` (Write to `i`)\n  - This operation is inside a for loop: `for (int k = 0; k < NUM; k++)`\n  - The loop condition `k < NUM` can be satisfied:\n    - `k` is initialized to 0\n    - `NUM` is defined as 20\n    - The loop will execute 20 times (k=0,1,2,...,19)\n  - Therefore, this write operation will be executed 20 times\n\n### Operations in svp_simple_332_001_isr_2:\n- **Line 20**: `j = i + 1;` (Read from `i`)\n  - This operation is inside a for loop: `for (int k = 0; k < NUM; k++)`\n  - The loop condition `k < NUM` can be satisfied:\n    - `k` is initialized to 0\n    - `NUM` is defined as 20\n    - The loop will execute 20 times (k=0,1,2,...,19)\n  - Therefore, this read operation will be executed 20 times\n\n### Operations in svp_simple_332_001_main:\n- **Line 26**: `int condI = i >= LIMIT;` (Read from `i`)\n  - This read operation is executed unconditionally in the main function\n- **Line 28**: `int condJ = j >= LIMIT;` (Read from `j`)\n  - This read operation is executed unconditionally in the main function\n- **Line 30**: `if (condI || condJ)` - the condition check uses the previously read values\n\n## Step 2: Check Interrupt Status\n\nThe code does not contain any `disable_isr()` or `enable_isr()` calls, which means:\n- Both ISRs (svp_simple_332_001_isr_1 and svp_simple_332_001_isr_2) can preempt the main function\n- The ISRs can also preempt each other based on their priorities (ISR 1 has priority 1, ISR 2 has priority 2)\n\n## Step 3: Analysis Summary\n\nThe reported atomicity violation involves:\n1. Write to `i` at line 14 (in ISR 1)\n2. Read from `i` at line 20 (in ISR 2)\n3. Write to `i` at line 14 (in ISR 1)\n\nAll these operations can be executed because:\n- The for loops in both ISRs will execute (20 iterations each)\n- There are no interrupt disable/enable calls preventing ISR execution\n- The ISRs can preempt each other and the main function\n\nThe pattern represents a classic atomicity violation where:\n- ISR 1 writes to `i`\n- ISR 2 reads from `i`\n- ISR 1 writes to `i` again\n- This creates a non-atomic sequence that could lead to inconsistent state\n\n```json\n{\n    \"violations\": [\n        {\n            \"sharedVariable\": \"i\",\n            \"accessPattern\": [\"Write\", \"Read\", \"Write\"],\n            \"lines\": [14, 20, 14]\n        }\n    ]\n}\n```\n\n[Expert R2] (Refine the report based on judge feedback, re-check for missed or false defects.)\n```json\n{\n    \"violations\": [\n        {\n            \"sharedVariable\": \"i\",\n            \"accessPattern\": [\"Write\", \"Read\", \"Write\"],\n            \"lines\": [14, 20, 14]\n        }\n    ]\n}\n```\n\n"
